; Post-repair AI board verification of the complete-root envelope and lower door.
import "../form/form-stdlib/core.fk"
import "review-panel.fk"
import "review-ask.fk"

(ra-review
  "docs/coherence-substrate/form-neutral-language-world-model.md"
  "Final independent verification; do not edit any file. The prior board found that the recursive element walk omitted the graph's packed-size and budget cells (64 bytes), and that direct graph construction recognized category without validating interior shape or linkage. Read model/form-neutral-language-world-model.fk and model/tests/form-neutral-language-world-model-band.fk plus their imported dictionary, crossing, world-model, and DS4 baseline cells. Freshly preflight and run the integration band. Construct an honest crossing and verify fnwm-graph-size equals a recursive fnwm-node-envelope-bytes walk from the returned graph root, including both header trivial cells. With a budget equal to a smaller full-root graph, verify a larger faithful surface/provenance/recipe rests outside. Try malformed but known-category symbols, relations, mappings, anchors, provenance, dangling relation endpoints, and mappings whose anchor symbol is absent; the public fnwm-graph door must return nothing. Recheck ordinary crossing, idempotent extension, bidirectional provenance query, world persistence/orientation, depth overflow, and DS4-specific size wording. Return PASS AS A BOUNDED WORLD-MODEL INTEGRATION, REVISE, or BLOCK with executable evidence. Empty or unfinished output is absence, not a vote.")
